{"name": "angband", "game": "Angband", "version": "0.0.0", "hidden": false, "groups": [{"name": "Game Options", "options": [{"name": "progression_balancing", "display_name": "Progression Balancing", "description": "A system that can move progression earlier, to try and prevent the player from getting stuck and bored early.\n\nA lower setting means more getting stuck. A higher setting means less getting stuck.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "NamedRange", "default": 50, "min": 0, "max": 99, "presets": {"disabled": 0, "normal": 50, "extreme": 99}}, {"name": "accessibility", "display_name": "Accessibility", "description": "Set rules for reachability of your items/locations.\n\n**Full:** ensure everything can be reached and acquired.\n\n**Minimal:** ensure what is needed to reach your goal can be acquired.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 0, "choices": [{"name": "full", "display_name": "Full", "value": 0}, {"name": "minimal", "display_name": "Minimal", "value": 2}]}], "collapsed": false}, {"name": "Gameplay Options", "options": [{"name": "artifacts_as_checks", "display_name": "Artifacts As Checks", "description": "Choose how artifacts interact with Archipelago.\n\n\"One to One\" (the default and the way the randomizer is balanced): every\nartifact is its own location check.  Picking up an artifact sends that\nartifact's check and the real artifacts are instead handed out by the\nmultiworld.  Descending past the early dungeon also requires having received\nenough \"Progressive ... Artifact\" items, so the artifacts gate progression.\n\n\"Accumulated\": artifacts are still handed out by the multiworld and still gate\ndescent exactly as in One to One, but the location checks are milestones -\n\"Find #X Artifacts\" - that fire on your X'th distinct artifact pickup no matter\nwhich artifacts you find.  The milestones are spread deeper the further you\ndescend (see the docs), reaching every artifact by the bottom.\n\n\"Off\": artifacts spawn and behave normally, only unique-monster kills are\nchecks, and the dungeon has no artifact gating.\n\nThe connected game reads this from slot_data (key \"artifacts_as_checks\":\n0 = Off, 1 = One to One, 2 = Accumulated).", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 1, "choices": [{"name": "off", "display_name": "Off", "value": 0}, {"name": "one_to_one", "display_name": "One To One", "value": 1}, {"name": "accumulated", "display_name": "Accumulated", "value": 2}]}, {"name": "resistances", "display_name": "Resistances", "description": "Choose how the character's power curve works.\n\n\"Standard\": normal Angband play.  Your equipment is whatever you find, and\n(if artifacts are checks) the multiworld hands out artifacts.\n\n\"Equipment Traits\": you cannot use artifacts and cannot equip anything except\na ranged weapon and a light source.  Instead you wield an unremovable\nArchipelago Weapon, and the multiworld items are traits that improve it:\nevery resistance, protections, to-hit/damage/dice/lightness, armor class,\nspeed, extra blows and three progressive slays.  The fire/cold/lightning/acid\nresists are progressive (resist, then an at-will temporary-resist activation,\nthen immunity).  Dungeon depth is gated on these traits instead of artifacts.\n\n\"Full Traits\": Equipment Traits, and additionally your character is switched\nto the Archipelago race - worst-in-everything - whose stats and skills are\nimproved by additional multiworld trait items.\n\nTrait modes replace the artifact items in the pool, so they require\nArtifacts As Checks to be On (One to One or Accumulated).\n\nThe connected game reads this from slot_data (key \"resistances\": 0 =\nStandard, 1 = Equipment Traits, 2 = Full Traits).", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 0, "choices": [{"name": "standard", "display_name": "Standard", "value": 0}, {"name": "equipment_traits", "display_name": "Equipment Traits", "value": 1}, {"name": "full_traits", "display_name": "Full Traits", "value": 2}]}, {"name": "black_market_price_multiplier", "display_name": "Black Market Price Multiplier", "description": "Price multiplier for the Black Market's \"buy a missed artifact location\"\ngold sink.\n\nWhile artifacts are checks (One to One or Accumulated), pressing $ in the\nBlack Market lets you spend gold to send an artifact location check you would\notherwise have to hunt for.  The cost is this multiplier times the artifact's\nbase value; a higher multiplier makes the gold sink more expensive.\n\nThe connected game reads this from slot_data (key\n\"black_market_price_multiplier\").  Has no effect when Artifacts As Checks is\nOff.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Range", "default": 3, "min": 1, "max": 5}, {"name": "death_link", "display_name": "Death Link", "description": "When you die, everyone who enabled death link dies. Of course, the reverse is true too.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Toggle", "default": false}], "collapsed": false}, {"name": "Item & Location Options", "options": [{"name": "local_items", "display_name": "Local Items", "description": "Forces these items to be in their native world.", "randomizable": false, "visibility": 15, "type": "OptionSet", "default": [], "options": ["Progressive Light Artifact", "Progressive Bladed Weapon Artifact", "Progressive Blunt Weapon Artifact", "Progressive Polearm Weapon Artifact", "Progressive Ranged Weapon Artifact", "Pick of Erebor", "Mattock of N\u00e1in", "Progressive Boots Artifact", "Progressive Helm Artifact", "Progressive Armor Artifact", "Progressive Cloak Artifact", "Progressive Gloves Artifact", "Progressive Shield Artifact", "Progressive Ring Artifact", "Progressive Amulet Artifact", "2 Potions of Augmentation", "+5 levels of Experience", "Rod of Recall", "Scroll of Acquirement", "Scroll of Deep Descent", "Triple Starting Gold", "Expanded Starting Shop Books", "Piece of Elvish Waybread", "Prog